   "record": "2aa18159549a41f9135273157b0a699abdfb3be6b4e06cf349973e6ddeef99de",
   "status": "UNCLEAR",
   "ruling": "Ruling: representation; the model asks whether a filer may deduct investment interest without Form 4952 and get zero. f4952 (2025) p. 3, Who Must File: \"you must file Form 4952 to claim a deduction for your investment interest expense. Exception. You don’t have to file Form 4952 if all of the following apply\" (investment income from interest and ordinary dividends less qualified dividends above the expense, no other deductible investment expenses, no 2024 carryover). Such a filer still has investment interest on Form 4952 line 1 above zero, so f4952.used is true and f4952.line8 is the smaller of lines 3 and 6, which under the exception's first condition is the whole interest: the form is used as the computation, whether or not it is filed (f4952.required). Line 8 is zero only with no investment interest, no carryforward and no election, when there is nothing to deduct. Inspected in forms/2025/f4952.yaml (f4952.used, f4952.line8) after PENDING-6 of the credits-misc package.",
   "subject_key": "f41626f3005cc062c5417cf28ba03d7d5ac2af971dcfbc1657c9dd4552e3e66d"
  },
